# truck-intel: DAILY refresh of mechanic detail (everything except Overture).
#
# THE SPLIT, AND WHY
# ------------------
# truckintel-mechanics.service runs monthly and does the expensive part: a
# national Overture Places parquet scan (~3 h) that discovers WHICH shops
# exist. Overture publishes monthly, so polling it faster would burn a national
# scan to rewrite identical rows and reset observed_at, making stale data look
# fresh.
#
# But the sources that fill in DETAIL about those shops change daily:
#   - NY/NJ licence registries      (Socrata, updated continuously)
#   - All The Places chain feeds    (re-scraped weekly)
#   - OpenStreetMap                 (edited continuously)
# Leaving those on the monthly schedule meant a shop could gain a licence
# record, opening hours, or an independent corroboration and we would not know
# for up to 31 days.
#
# `--refresh` is the whole pipeline MINUS the Overture pull. Minutes, not hours.
#
# It ends with a fill report: per-field coverage plus the delta since the last
# run, so a day that learned nothing is visibly different from a day that
# learned something. Without that, a refresh which silently stopped finding
# detail would look exactly like one that is working.
#
# CONCURRENCY: on the 2nd of each month this and the monthly pull are both due.
# mechanic_list.py takes a Postgres advisory lock for its whole run and exits 0
# with a "[skip]" line if another run holds it, so the two can never interleave
# a TRUNCATE+reload with UPDATEs. Timing them apart is not a guarantee — a slow
# pull outlives any gap — so the lock is the guarantee and the clock is only a
# courtesy.
[Unit]
Description=truck-intel daily mechanic detail refresh (licence + chains + OSM + verify)
After=network-online.target docker.service truckintel-osm-truck-repair.service
Wants=network-online.target

[Service]
Type=oneshot
WorkingDirectory=%h/Documents/truck-intel
# Measured ~4 min: two Socrata registry pulls (22.8k rows), five All The Places
# spiders, an OSM spatial join, 11.7k re-scores, the CBP denominator and the
# HTML render. The ceiling is for a slow upstream, not for normal work.
TimeoutStartSec=45m
ExecStart=%h/.local/bin/uv run python scripts/mechanic_list.py --refresh
Nice=10
IOSchedulingClass=idle
